\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Reward model}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{reward-model}
\tag{preference}

\p{A \strong{reward model} is a parameterized score
#{\widehat r_\phi(x,y)\in\mathbb R}. Write
#{\sigma(u)=(1+\exp(-u))^{-1}}. Under the Bradley--Terry observation model,
the pairwise loss is}

##{
 L_{\mathrm{rm}}(\phi)
 =\mathbb E_{(x,y^+,y^-)\sim\mathcal D_{\mathrm{pref}}}
 \left[-\log\sigma\left(
   \widehat r_\phi(x,y^+)-\widehat r_\phi(x,y^-)
 \right)\right].
}

\p{Section 3.5, Equation (1), and Appendix C.2 of
\citef{ouyang2022training} use this pairwise reward-model loss. It is a
method-specific scalar representation of pairwise data. General or cyclic
preferences need not admit such a representation.}
